In the system which will be sharing files (ubuntu):
1.apdate & install samba protocol
 sudo apt apdate 
 sudo apt install samba

2.check the server and enable, disable, status, start, stop the service
 sudo systemctl check smbd

3.Now create a directory you want to share and set permission to 777
 mkdir SHARE
 chmod 777 SHARE

4.Edit the configure file to share the directory
 sudo nano /etc/samba/smb.conf
 find -name smb.conf   \\If you don't know the location

5.now write the permissions and path to access the directory
   [Shared]
  path = /srv/samba/shared 
  browseable = yes
  read only = no
  writable = yes
  guest ok = no
  valid users = yourusername
  create mask = 0664
  directory mask = 0775

6.Set the password for user to access the smbd directory
 sudo smbpasswd -a username \\-a is to add our user to samba user database

Now go to the system which is going to access the smb directory (windows):
1.find the ip address
 hostname -I

2.open fileexplorer and enter
 \\ipaddress\SHARED directory name
